# Rust build output. cargo-guard keeps ONE shared target directory per repo at
# <repo-root>/target/claude, so ignoring `target/` at any depth covers that and
# a plain local compile inside rust/ as well.
target/

# The prebuilt Rust binary, copied into the host checkout by hand: neither mini
# has a toolchain. Ignored so it never reads as an untracked change — a host
# `git pull` stays silent, and nobody is tempted to `git clean -xdf` the
# running service out of existence.
/asr-backend-rs
# The previous build, kept beside it as an on-host rollback. Same class, same
# reason: on 2026-11-14 an untracked one made host-config-sync report the mini2
# checkout DIRTY and stop deploying it ("stays frozen until the worktree is
# clean") — a binary artifact must never be able to freeze a deploy.
/asr-backend-rs.prev
